From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] Plutonium: DRM: shell mode on the display hardware

Running on the hardware: the display-plane path, logind seats (also on a VT that isn't in front), evdev and libinput fixes, touchpad swipes for the shell, and the GPU details (Vulkan device ids, the GPU's PCI ids without libpci, shm buffers the GPU can't import).

It holds these changes:
- set the DRM device id for a Vulkan device shared with ANGLE
- the GPUs' PCI ids from sysfs where ANGLE has none (no libpci): the GPU list's exceptions match, and GPU rasterization isn't blocklisted
- seat management through logind
- shm buffers the GPU can't import don't stall the display; EXO-DIAG logs at VLOG(1)
- start a logind session on a VT that isn't in front
- a detached input device's settings update runs on the UI thread
- touchpad swipes with three fingers or more go to the shell page

and the parts in these files of:
- Exo embedding (Phase 1) and window broker (Phase 2)
- shell mode on DRM, evdev input fix, display-plane path
- browser tabs as SurfaceEmbed elements, DRM mouse wheel
- niri shell keys, touchpad and scrolling, drag and drop, shell links as tabs
